WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:13.242
Hi! Prepositions tell us about time and place, and conjunctions join two ideas together. They are short words, but easy to get wrong. Let's learn them today.

2
00:00:13.392 --> 00:00:18.234
Use at for a clock time: school starts at 7.30 a.m.

3
00:00:18.384 --> 00:00:26.058
Use on for days and dates. Her birthday is on 4 October. The library is closed on Sundays.

4
00:00:26.208 --> 00:00:32.778
Use in for months, years, seasons and parts of the day. We visit our cousins in December.

5
00:00:32.928 --> 00:00:42.930
Some prepositions go with certain words, and we learn them together: good at drawing, afraid of the dark, interested in music, proud of you.

6
00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:51.114
And adds an idea, but shows a contrast, or gives a choice, and so shows a result: it rained, so we stayed home.

7
00:00:51.264 --> 00:01:00.306
Because gives a reason: Ken was late because he missed the bus. Although shows something unexpected: although it was cold, she went for a swim.

8
00:01:00.456 --> 00:01:07.386
When, before, after and until are about time: wash your hands before you eat.

9
00:01:07.536 --> 00:01:12.474
Watch out! Although and but must not be used in the same sentence!

10
00:01:12.624 --> 00:01:17.850
Say: although it rained, we played. Or: it rained, but we played.

11
00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:23.874
The same goes for because and so. Use only one of them.

12
00:01:24.024 --> 00:01:34.674
Your turn! Her birthday is, ___, 4 October. In, on or at? Pause and think.

13
00:01:34.824 --> 00:01:43.962
On. We use on for a date. If we only gave the month, we would say in October. Did you get it right?

14
00:01:44.112 --> 00:01:55.242
Another one! Raju is very good, ___, drawing animals. Which preposition? Pause and think.

15
00:01:55.392 --> 00:02:05.994
At. Good at is a fixed phrase, like bad at, afraid of and interested in. We learn them as whole phrases. Did you get it right?

16
00:02:06.144 --> 00:02:16.482
Next one! I was tired, ___, I went to bed early. But, so or or? Pause and think.

17
00:02:16.632 --> 00:02:24.666
So. Being tired is the reason, and going to bed early is the result. Did you get it right?

18
00:02:24.816 --> 00:02:34.842
Last one! ___, it was late, Dad kept working. Because or although? Pause and think.

19
00:02:34.992 --> 00:02:42.738
Although. It was late, yet he kept working, which is unexpected. Did you get it right?

20
00:02:42.888 --> 00:02:52.506
Remember: at for clock times, on for days and dates, in for months, years and parts of the day. Learn phrases like good at and afraid of as a whole.

21
00:02:52.656 --> 00:03:02.562
For conjunctions, think about how the two ideas link: and to add, but for contrast, so for a result, because for a reason, although for a surprise.

22
00:03:02.712 --> 00:03:07.794
Today, tell your family a sentence with because in it!

